 thoughts into Latin and expressing them in real human-to-human interaction allows one to experience the unique structural, grammatical, and syntactical features of the language actively and not just passively. This will in turn enhance reading comprehension. Thus this course will always draw inspiration from real authors and real texts, including Plautus, Cicero, Jerome, Erasmus, and many others.", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "This course does not count toward the A&S language requirement.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: One year of college-level Latin or its equivalent.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2678, "crseId": 353621, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LATIN", "catalogNbr": "3204", "titleShort": "Roman Prose", "titleLong": "Roman Prose", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16000, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:40AM", "timeEnd": "09:55AM", "startDt": "08/22/2017", "endDt": "12/01/2017", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "dbg223", "firstName": "Daniel", "middleName": "B.", "lastName": "Gallagher"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall 158", "bldgDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "GSH158", "meetingTopicDescription": null}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Prerequisite - 2000-level Latin class."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2017", "end